  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Cover of grey cardboard, printed on pages 1 and 4, with slits cut into which yellow paper pieces are held in place on the interior (pages 2 and 3 of cover). Yellow paper piece in shape of a shoe in the back. In the front, yellow paper with two cutouts (one of which is on the inner back cover) has picture printed and text in red and black with text by Andrés Grillo. Inside, four sheets of paper are folded to form the body of the volume. Red, blue, brown, and black papers held in place by tied white cord. Red sheet printed in black on both sides. Between red and blue sheets printed in black, a painted band made of a newspaper clipping. On side of blue sheet facing the red one, the lettering continues the message on the red sheet and spells out Pacifistas Violentamente Asesinados. On side of blue sheet that faces the brown pages, prints in blue ink appear. Brown pages contain text by Javiera Medina. Black pages have cut-out forms. In the very center, lighter-weight paper is printed on both sides with photographic reproduction of shoe boxes at shoe store on one side, and photograph of shelves with some eyeglasses, tools, a shoe last, a tin of Nescafé, a few shoes, and small round containers with what seem to be nails within.</subfield>
  </datafield>
